---
import MovieFlexLegalLayout from "../layouts/MovieFlexLegalLayout.astro";
---

<MovieFlexLegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What MovieFlex stores, what it sends to data providers, and how to control your local data."
  eyebrow="PRIVACY"
>
  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <p>
    MovieFlex is a movie-discovery interface. It lets you search titles, view
    metadata, and check reported streaming availability. The current version
    does not require an account.
  </p>
  <div class="legal-note">
    The watchlist and privacy choice are stored in your browser. MovieFlex does
    not currently install analytics or advertising trackers.
  </div>
  <h2>Information processed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Searches and filters:</strong> the movie title, list, genre, page,
      or country you choose is sent to the MovieFlex API endpoint so it can
      request the relevant data from TMDB.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Watchlist:</strong> saved movie IDs and basic display details are
      stored in your browser's local storage on this device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy choice:</strong> a small local-storage entry remembers
      that you selected essential-only storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical requests:</strong> the browser and server may process
      standard connection information needed to deliver pages and API responses.
      Hosting and network providers may maintain their own logs.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Data sources</h2>
  <p>
    Movie metadata and poster images are supplied by TMDB. Streaming
    availability is returned through TMDB using data powered by JustWatch. When
    your browser loads third-party images or you follow an external link, those
    services may receive technical information under their own policies.
  </p>
  <h2>How data is used</h2>
  <p>
    Data is used to return search results, display movie details and reported
    availability, save your on-device list, and remember your privacy setting.
    The current version does not use your searches for advertising or analytics
    profiling.
  </p>
  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Your watchlist remains in this browser until you remove saved titles or
    clear this site's local storage. Use{" "}
    <a href="/privacy-settings">Privacy settings</a> to clear the watchlist.
    Clearing site data in your browser also removes the saved list and local
    privacy choice.
  </p>
  <h2>Children and sensitive information</h2>
  <p>
    MovieFlex is not designed to collect personal profiles or sensitive personal
    information. Do not submit sensitive information in search fields.
  </p>
  <h2>Third-party sites</h2>
  <p>
    TMDB, JustWatch, and streaming providers operate independently. Once you
    leave MovieFlex, their terms and privacy notices apply to your interactions
    with them.
  </p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    This notice may be updated as the project changes. This is a portfolio
    project; no dedicated privacy contact address has been configured yet. For
    questions, use the contact method published by the project owner on the
    portfolio site.
  </p>
</MovieFlexLegalLayout>
